20 years ago I did research and I showed  what I called the compromise effect  whereby depending on what products you  you place in front of consumers they  tend to take the middle option well a  year ago a doctoral student here at  Stanford Tali wife and I conducted a  study where we try to replicate that  compromise effect this time however we  showed the participants some of the  information that's available on Amazon  we showed them some other cameras the  same product categories we used back in  1992 and we show them reviews so we  showed them some of the information  available to consumers today what  happened  the compromise effect disappeared and  that's really the essence of what has  changed from making decisions in  relative terms in the old days where you  make decisions based on the set of  options that is placed in front of you  to the way you make decisions today  which means that today you no longer  have to rely on what marketers choose to  show you  the new reality is one where the key is  the absolute value that you provide  customers customers will rely much more  on what others are saying and much less  on their past history with your product  about the brand or about the fact that  your product was placed in the movies or  it had the recommend being recommended  by some celebrity they really rely on  what others are saying which in many  categories simply reflects more or less  the truth and you're likely experienced  with that product even though you hear  all those mantras even today that brands  have never been more important and the  best investment a marketer can make is  in loyalty we disagree we feel that  actually the important of loyalty and  brands and persuasion is diminishing and  to the extent that your customers can  assess quality directly spending money  on persuasion for example through  advertising may be a waste of money  one good way to do it is to go with the  product itself to focus on the product  itself you know if you view some  commercials for some of the high-tech  companies now that promote phones and  they really feature specific they look  at the highlight the the specific  features they create interest through  reviews there are a different method to  seed product to encourage influencers to  talk about the product again in a  totally authentic and honest way but  it's much more focused on product than  brand  instead of measuring consumers existing  preferences to predict the future  preferences you have to recognize the  reality where consumers make decisions  today based on reviews that are  available today which means that what  you need to do is to find out what  reviewers are saying today who are the  most influential reviewers and how can  we help them recognize the absolute  value of our products in the old days  and unjust  perhaps ten years ago marketers were  very much in control they could decide  what products to show consumers they  could build a brand's and as they did  they could invest in loyalty and they  could spend money on advertising which  was effective in inducing purchase  decisions today all those tools are  becoming less important marketers are  much less in control and they need to  determine where they are go along with  their situation in terms of the way  their customers are making decisions  there is no way for marketers to change  that because that is the way consumers  are making decisions today and there's  really no way back
 

